  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted ((EX)000, (EX)180, (EX)400, (EX)410, (EX)420, (PL)108, (PL)400, (PL)410, (PL)420, covering letter dated 19 June 2020 and Design and Access Statement dated 08 June 2020 Rev 2. Received: 22 June 2020\r\nZero-Carbon Technical Note dated 12 August 2020. Received: 12 August 2020 \r\nEnergy Statement dated October 2020. Received: 09 October 2020. ) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - Prior to commencement of development the applicant shall have entered into a formal agreement with the Council to provide a payment of ?4560.00 towards its Carbon Offset Fund.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 5 - A) The development shall be implemented in strict accordance with the approved Energy Strategy and any subsequent revision. \r\n\r\nB) Prior to first occupation of the building(s) evidence (e.g.\r\nphotographs, installation contracts and As-Built certificates under\r\nthe Standard Assessment Procedure) should be submitted to the\r\nLocal Planning Authority and approved in writing to show that the\r\ndevelopment has been constructed in accordance with the\r\napproved Energy Strategy, and any subsequent approved revisions.\r\n\r\nC) Upon final commencement of operation of the air source heat pumps suitable devices for the monitoring of the pumps shall have been installed and the monitored data shall be submitted automatically to a monitoring web-platform at daily intervals for a period of three years from the point of full operation.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to occupation of the hereby approved development the private amenity space as shown on the approved plans shall be provided and be ready for use by the occupant of the flats and shall be retained as such for the duration of the development.",
    "Condition : 7 - The flat labelled L7.04 on the submitted plans shall be for single occupation only and shall not be permanently occupied by more than a single occupant at any time for the duration of the development.",
    "Condition : 8 - Suitable measures shall be incorporated into the hereby approved development to ensure that the proposed dwellings do not experience noise levels that exceed the standards set out in BS 8233:2014.",
    "Condition : 9 - Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, the Local Planning Authority shall be informed of the agreed naming and numbering of the proposed dwellings so that arrangements can be put in place to ensure that, with the exception of a person eligible for a disabled person's badge issued pursuant to section 21 of the Chronically Sick and Disabled Persons Act 1970 (or similar legislation), no resident of the development shall obtain a resident's parking permit. Any occupiers of the approved development shall surrender any such permit wrongly issued or held.",
    "Condition : 10 - Prior to the occupation of the hereby approved development the cycle parking and bin store area shall be provided in accordance with the approved plans and be ready for use and retained as such for the duration of the development without obstruction."
  ],
